issue.body:
Given code like

```java
package simons.client;

import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.io.InputStreamReader;
import java.net.URL;

public class Main
{
    public static void main( String... a ) throws IOException
    {
        var url = new URL( "resource:foo/bar.txt" );
        try ( var is = new BufferedReader( new InputStreamReader( url.openStream() ) ) )
        {
            is.lines().forEach( System.out::println );
        }
    }
}
```

following https://www.graalvm.org/22.0/reference-manual/native-image/URLProtocols/ using the `resource` protocol together with a config 

```json
{
  "resources": [
    {
      "pattern": "foo/bar\\.txt"
    }
  ]
}
```

triggered by 

```
Args = -H:ResourceConfigurationResources=${.}/resources-config.json
```

in a `native-image.properties` used to work in GraalVM 21.3.0, printing out the content of the given text file.

GraalVM 22.1.0 throws:

```
Exception in thread "main" java.io.FileNotFoundException: resource:foo/bar.txt
	at com.oracle.svm.core.jdk.resources.ResourceURLConnection.getInputStream(ResourceURLConnection.java:91)
	at java.net.URL.openStream(URL.java:1161)
	at simons.client.Main.main(Main.java:13)
```

**Steps to reproduce the issue**

```
curl -OL https://github.com/oracle/graal/files/8573481/some-client.zip
unzip some-client.zip 
cd some-client
mvn package  
./target/some-client
```

GraalVM 21.3.0 prints `Hello, GraalVM rocks.`, GraalVM 22.1.0 fails.

**Describe GraalVM and your environment:**
- GraalVM 22.1.0 Java 17 CE (Java Version 17.0.3+7-jvmci-22.1-b06)
 - OS: macOS 12.2.1 
 - X86_64

Feels related to this comment:
https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/22097#issuecomment-99805528

Reproducer [here](https://github.com/oracle/graal/files/8573481/some-client.zip) (see "Steps to reproduce the issue"). Thanks @fniephaus
